flickos-greeter (2.0~test2) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Phase 2 of the login screen: Shut Down and Restart with a second
    click, through logind (a block inhibitor is named on the card), the
    keyboard layout while there is more than one (cage changes it; two
    layouts always get a switch key), and zoom with Super+=, Super+-,
    Super+0 and Super+scroll, remembered at login. The text is ready for
    translation (po/).

 -- Jon <dvbondoy@gmail.com>  Thu, 05 Nov 2026 10:11:45 +0800

flickos-greeter (2.0~test1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * FlickOS's own login screen (greeter-window, docs/design/flickos-
    greeter.md phase 1): the users with their pictures or initials, the
    last one picked, a password box that can show the password, and the
    sessions by name (FlickOS, FlickOS (Plain Session), other Wayland
    sessions but bare labwc), each user's last one picked again.
    gtkgreet comes up when it can't start. The login screen's output
    goes to the journal (journalctl -b -t flickos-greeter). Breaks
    flickos-recovery before 1.6, which didn't count this login screen as
    a start that worked.

 -- Jon <dvbondoy@gmail.com>  Wed, 04 Nov 2026 21:43:39 +0800

